-- title:
--   The arguments of a batched query satisfy the precondition of the query core
-- statement:
--   Let $t\le m$, the limits satisfy `Lim30 lim p t b0 U`, the input arrays $A_L$, $A_R$ be bounded by $U$ (`BoundA`), and the memory $\mu$ hold the data structure `DSReadyA p t aX aY b0 AL AR` of Theorem 30 for these arrays. For positions $I,J<N$ whose output-digit string is stored at `aWD p b0`, the argument list `coreArgsA p t hmL b0 AL AR μ I J` of the query core satisfies its precondition `QueryCorePreP lim μ` (the tries of the bands of $I$ and $J$, their roots, the box and the work areas are where the query core of Theorem 30 expects them).
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Batch/QueryA.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2995561_Defs1 and APSP2995561_Defs2 (and APSP2996001_Defs1-2, APSP299791_Defs1-5 of the earlier entries). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (revised 7 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Theorem 30 for arbitrary input arrays.

